1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,841
- Someone stood out to me.
- Who?

2
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:51,426
That Rahmboy.

3
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:57,182
<i>Be careful.</i>

4
00:00:57,265 --> 00:00:58,600
<i>Especially around Agent Alex.</i>

5
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:01,394
<i>Nothing changes in the plan.</i>
<i>We're going through with it.</i>

6
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:07,442
Oh, and Chiara asked me
to give this to you.

7
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:26,252
I'm really getting stressed out
because of that GAGO.

8
00:01:30,673 --> 00:01:33,593
I don't want them to be
the only ones having fun.

9
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:39,015
But seriously.

10
00:01:47,148 --> 00:01:49,109
I really thought

11
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:52,112
you wouldn't be able to make it
to my wedding.

12
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:04,874
She's so beautiful, Viktor. Look at her.

13
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:15,135
This means so much to me, having you here.

14
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:18,888
This might just be the best wedding gift
I could ask for.

15
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:22,684
Don't ruin my makeup.

16
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:26,938
Actually, we should be the ones
thanking you.

17
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:31,526
Didn't you tell me before
that everything is possible?

18
00:02:33,111 --> 00:02:36,573
Because of all your sacrifices,

19
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:38,825
for staying with the agency,

20
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:48,167
Your sacrifices were definitely worth it,

21
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:49,544
even with the case your father and I have.

22
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:54,132
It's okay because they understood
that we're your parents.

23
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,680
then why are you still hurt?

24
00:03:01,347 --> 00:03:02,432
Don't worry.

25
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:17,155
I knew he wasn't really
a true public servant.

26
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:18,281
Calm down.

27
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:22,285
It's your wedding. Don't stress.

28
00:03:22,368 --> 00:03:23,786
- Don't stress, okay?
- Yes.

29
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:33,463
I feel so bad
that there's nothing I can do.

30
00:03:34,047 --> 00:03:35,381
Don't, daughter.

31
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:37,300
We'll handle it, please.

32
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:40,845
Just focus on being happy.

33
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:43,681
We're here to celebrate!

34
00:03:44,682 --> 00:03:45,558
Yay!

35
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:50,063
- Thank you!
- I’m getting married!

36
00:04:01,532 --> 00:04:03,910
Mama Yaya? You mean,

37
00:04:04,702 --> 00:04:06,371
La Morte Bianca's Mama Yaya?

38
00:04:06,454 --> 00:04:08,873
Your nanny when you trained in Sicily?

39
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:12,377
What is she doing here?

40
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:15,463
She's from Albay too?

41
00:04:15,546 --> 00:04:18,132
And she just happens
to show up for your wedding?

42
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:20,134
How's Vicky?

43
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:23,096
What's her plan here?

44
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:32,563
Well, whatever Mama Yaya's plan is,

45
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:34,732
that's for her to decide.

46
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:46,327
If there's anything
I've learned all these years,

47
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:53,061
<i>Even when it's difficult.</i>

48
00:05:55,104 --> 00:05:56,647
<i>Even when it's complicated.</i>

49
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:36,896
<i>And even when the situation</i>
<i>is sometimes frightening.</i>

50
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:41,400
<i>But when you love someone,</i>

51
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:45,780
<i>you have to be wholehearted</i>
<i>and sincere in your intentions.</i>

52
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:53,496
<i>That the decision you make</i>

53
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:56,457
<i>is for the good of the people you love.</i>

54
00:07:09,387 --> 00:07:11,264
<i>Love wears many faces.</i>

55
00:07:25,069 --> 00:07:27,780
<i>There are many ways to care</i>

56
00:07:27,864 --> 00:07:29,574
<i>and many ways to sacrifice.</i>

57
00:08:07,111 --> 00:08:11,616
<i>But why do we always have to choose?</i>

58
00:08:17,288 --> 00:08:19,457
<i>There's always a decision to make.</i>

59
00:09:05,253 --> 00:09:07,922
<i>And when we make our decisions,</i>

60
00:09:09,173 --> 00:09:11,968
<i>we try to choose what's right.</i>

61
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:29,986
<i>We try to do everything we can</i>
<i>to make things right.</i>

62
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:49,589
<i>And until the very end,</i>

63
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:55,845
<i>I will choose to love in the only way</i>
<i>I know how.</i>

64
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:59,849
<i>For the person I love most.</i>

65
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:34,443
Mr. Mikoy Pinagpala, I will marry you.

66
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:40,241
And I will stay by your side
until my very last breath.

67
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:50,644
MJ.

68
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:57,651
Why is it taking so long
for the door to open?

69
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:03,616
MJ?

70
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:04,950
MJ.

71
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:07,453
Why is the bride taking so long?

72
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:33,896
Agent Alex is running?

73
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:02,258
Where's Chiara?

74
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:03,676
Why hasn't she come out yet?

75
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:05,344
I don't know either.

76
00:14:05,427 --> 00:14:08,264
Maybe there was just a small problem?

77
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:10,724
It can't be a small problem.

78
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:13,978
Let's all calm down first.

79
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:15,980
Stay calm.

80
00:14:29,577 --> 00:14:31,537
It's ringing, but no one's answering.

81
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:40,629
Oh my God!

82
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:41,589
What happened?

83
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:44,967
Brother Nanding! Brother Nanding!

84
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:46,302
Where is she?

85
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:47,761
What happened?

86
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:49,555
Sir!

87
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:52,683
MJ! Where's Chiara?

88
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:54,768
Ma'am, I don't know.

89
00:14:57,229 --> 00:14:59,273
What’s happening?
Everyone's just guessing.

90
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:02,610
I'm already sweating my ass off here!

91
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:04,028
Is the wedding still happening?

92
00:15:04,111 --> 00:15:06,822
Of course it is. After everything
that's happened, of course it is.

93
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,035
Oh, no.

94
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:14,204
Nanding! Oh my God! Oh my God!

95
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,169
Where is she?

96
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:23,255
Is our Internet connection
the only problem?

97
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:25,507
It looks like it's not, sir.

98
00:15:26,091 --> 00:15:28,677
This doesn't look like
a simple connection problem.

99
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:30,012
Any update on that?

100
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:34,183
I'm calling Agent Alex,
but she's not answering.

101
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:37,519
Okay, hold on.
I'll check with Carlota too.

102
00:15:49,823 --> 00:15:51,158
It's ringing, but no one's answering.

103
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:53,452
Mikoy.

104
00:15:53,535 --> 00:15:55,079
Chiara is missing.

105
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:56,455
She's not in the bridal car either.

106
00:15:57,873 --> 00:15:58,707
Are you sure?

107
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:01,210
Where's Chiara?

108
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:03,796
Maybe she just went to the bathroom.

109
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:06,006
Or maybe she forgot something
and went back to the hotel.

110
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:07,424
That's possible.

111
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:09,134
It's possible, but…

112
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:10,970
I'm going to find Chiara.

113
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:13,847
- Let's take a look.
- What's going on?

114
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:16,600
- Mikoy!
- Hey!

115
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:20,771
- Come--
- Mikoy!

116
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:23,065
Mikoy!

117
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:42,042
<i>Thank you so, so much for this day.</i>

118
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,920
<i>Please guide us.</i>

119
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:47,589
<i>I know you won't abandon us.</i>

120
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:52,845
<i>You alone know what is meant to happen</i>

121
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:55,848
<i>and when the time is right.</i>

122
00:16:56,598 --> 00:16:58,684
What do you mean Chiara
is missing? What happened?

123
00:16:59,351 --> 00:17:01,311
They said Chiara isn't in the bridal car.

124
00:17:02,104 --> 00:17:04,023
They can't get ahold of the driver either.

125
00:17:05,274 --> 00:17:06,775
They can't get ahold of the driver?

126
00:17:08,444 --> 00:17:09,278
Wait.

127
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:11,030
What's going on, Carlota?

128
00:17:12,197 --> 00:17:13,699
According to the wedding planner,

129
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:16,243
the driver was unconscious.

130
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:57,242
Everything scheduled
for each hour went as planned.

131
00:17:58,077 --> 00:18:01,622
That is, until a few minutes
before the bridal march.

132
00:18:01,705 --> 00:18:02,956
<i>Oddly,</i>

133
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:05,793
<i>it took a while for the door to open.</i>

134
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:10,130
before everyone started to worry.

135
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:12,132
<i>I immediately followed the wedding planner</i>

136
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:13,884
<i>to personally check on Chiara.</i>

137
00:18:14,551 --> 00:18:17,930
At first, we thought the bridal car driver
was unconscious.

138
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:19,765
But it turned out
he had just fallen asleep.

139
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:21,558
He just fell asleep?

140
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,312
Could someone have made him fall asleep?

141
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:32,903
So we didn't let it go.
We interrogated him.

142
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:37,950
Nanding, it's impossible for you
to just fall asleep while you're at work.

143
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:40,911
I don't know either, ma'am.

144
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:42,371
I just suddenly fell asleep.

145
00:18:43,038 --> 00:18:45,374
Nanding, what's the last thing
you remember before you fell asleep?

146
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:48,460
Ma'am, we arrived here,

147
00:18:50,087 --> 00:18:51,380
and as soon as I got here,

148
00:18:51,463 --> 00:18:53,006
I passed out. I fell asleep.

149
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:55,217
I don't remember what happened after that.

150
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:58,887
Did Chiara say anything
before you stopped here at the church?

151
00:18:59,471 --> 00:19:00,722
No, sir.

152
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:02,349
She didn't say anything to me.

153
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:06,395
My head still hurts badly even now.

154
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:18,157
The bride wasn't coming
from that far away from the church.

155
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:28,250
So? Why did the driver fall asleep?

156
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:33,672
We checked his car, sir.

157
00:19:33,755 --> 00:19:35,924
It looks like the smart car
scent diffuser was the trigger,

158
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:37,259
which caused him to fall asleep.

159
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:39,136
So how?

160
00:19:39,219 --> 00:19:42,931
Did someone put sleeping agents
in the scent before the wedding?

161
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:45,601
If someone put the driver to sleep,

162
00:19:46,685 --> 00:19:49,313
does that mean Chiara was kidnapped?

163
00:19:57,529 --> 00:19:59,031
Chiara could have been
the one who sprayed it.

164
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:01,491
Why would she do that?

165
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:08,165
Could she have gotten cold feet
at the last minute

166
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:09,666
and wanted to run away?

167
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:14,630
that does happen.

168
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:18,717
That seems impossible.

169
00:20:20,636 --> 00:20:22,512
After everything they've been through,

170
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:25,557
would she really have doubts now?

171
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:33,023
if she has an issue or a concern,
she'll tell you about it directly.

172
00:20:34,483 --> 00:20:36,526
If she had any doubts before the wedding,

173
00:20:37,694 --> 00:20:41,323
I'm sure she would've brought them up
with Mikoy so they could talk about it.

174
00:20:42,407 --> 00:20:44,409
That's exactly what Mikoy said too, sir.

175
00:20:44,993 --> 00:20:46,995
Even when their preparations
got stressful,

176
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:50,165
they were open and transparent
with each other.

177
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:52,584
And they made sure to discuss everything.

178
00:20:57,381 --> 00:21:00,092
we know that she's the kind of person

179
00:21:00,175 --> 00:21:04,972
who can make decisions and make moves
without telling anyone.

180
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:09,559
Chiara has a history of doing that.

181
00:21:10,852 --> 00:21:11,979
But this is different.

182
00:21:12,813 --> 00:21:14,815
This was supposed to be
her wedding to Mikoy.

183
00:21:14,898 --> 00:21:17,276
<i>This was something</i>
<i>they prepared for together.</i>

184
00:21:18,568 --> 00:21:22,197
It seems out of character for her
to suddenly make a move on her own.

185
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:27,411
<i>We also talked to everyone</i>
<i>who interacted with Chiara.</i>

186
00:21:27,494 --> 00:21:28,870
From the glam team,

187
00:21:28,954 --> 00:21:31,415
the person who made
her gown, the photographer,

188
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:34,459
all the hotel staff
who were on duty that morning.

189
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:37,379
Even all the guests who saw her.

190
00:21:38,213 --> 00:21:40,549
None of them noticed anything unusual.

191
00:21:40,632 --> 00:21:43,552
In fact, they all said the same thing.

192
00:21:44,094 --> 00:21:48,890
That Chiara was a beautiful
and excited bride.

193
00:21:49,891 --> 00:21:52,436
What time was the last time
you saw Chiara?

194
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:55,897
Actually, I was with her
about 30 minutes ago.

195
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:58,984
We even double-checked her dress.

196
00:21:59,067 --> 00:22:01,361
Then I helped her into the car.

197
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:03,697
What did you notice about her mindset,
about how she was feeling?

198
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:05,574
Was she happy? Sad? Angry?

199
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:08,243
She was so happy,
really excited about her dress.

200
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:10,996
She was so excited.
I don't know, my goodness!

201
00:22:11,079 --> 00:22:13,999
Did you leave her there,
or did she leave the place herself?

202
00:22:14,082 --> 00:22:16,835
Once she got into the bridal car,

203
00:22:16,918 --> 00:22:17,794
that was it.

204
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:18,712
- That was the last time we saw her.
- That was the last time you saw her.

205
00:22:18,795 --> 00:22:20,047
How many minutes ago was that?

206
00:22:21,548 --> 00:22:23,717
Aside from going to Mikoy's house,

207
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:27,054
we also checked the CCTV footage
from the church and the hotel.

208
00:22:35,437 --> 00:22:37,397
<i>But Chiara never returned to the hotel.</i>

209
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:39,691
<i>And she never got</i>
<i>out of the bridal car either.</i>

210
00:22:50,243 --> 00:22:54,706
Mario also helped us ask around for help.

211
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:58,043
In case they saw anything
or noticed anything unusual.

212
00:22:58,126 --> 00:23:01,755
You don't have any leads
or anything from your informants?

213
00:23:02,339 --> 00:23:03,548
I'm sorry, Mario,

214
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:06,218
but as of now, we can't say that

215
00:23:06,301 --> 00:23:08,136
Chiara Valtrovi is a missing person.

216
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:10,013
That's because of the 24-hour window.

217
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:12,849
But a lot can happen within 24 hours.

218
00:23:12,933 --> 00:23:14,643
We can't just sit around and do nothing.

219
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:16,645
With all due respect, Mario,

220
00:23:17,187 --> 00:23:19,439
this could be a case of a runaway bride.

221
00:23:19,523 --> 00:23:20,899
And besides, Mario,

222
00:23:20,982 --> 00:23:24,444
it's no secret that the bride was once
part of the mafia.

223
00:23:25,028 --> 00:23:27,614
Maybe, you know,

224
00:23:27,697 --> 00:23:29,616
she went back to her old life.

225
00:23:31,535 --> 00:23:34,079
It's not officially confirmed yet that

226
00:23:34,162 --> 00:23:36,373
Chiara is a missing person.

227
00:23:36,456 --> 00:23:37,791
What's important is,

228
00:23:37,874 --> 00:23:40,043
all the police have been alerted
at every checkpoint

229
00:23:40,127 --> 00:23:42,254
to watch out for Chiara.

230
00:23:42,337 --> 00:23:44,798
We also spoke to Donabel and Viktor.

231
00:23:45,423 --> 00:23:48,176
They spoke as a family
before Chiara left the hotel.

232
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:49,886
Papa Vik.

233
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:51,429
Mama Donabel.

234
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:53,265
How was your conversation with Chiara?

235
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:56,560
It was okay, Mikoy.

236
00:23:56,643 --> 00:23:58,436
Just a brief catch-up.

237
00:24:03,775 --> 00:24:04,860
Yes.

238
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:07,445
Our little reunion was cut short.

239
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:10,699
Did she mention anything
that was bothering her?

240
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:12,951
Or did you notice anything unusual
about her?

241
00:24:13,785 --> 00:24:14,911
Nothing.

242
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:17,455
Chiara actually seemed so happy.

243
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:19,374
And she even said, didn't she, that

244
00:24:19,457 --> 00:24:21,877
love is ultimately a decision.

245
00:24:22,794 --> 00:24:24,129
So,

246
00:24:24,212 --> 00:24:26,673
she was completely committed
to marrying you.

247
00:24:26,756 --> 00:24:28,717
To spend the rest of her life with you.

248
00:24:29,593 --> 00:24:31,094
Viktor, what happened to our daughter?

249
00:24:31,178 --> 00:24:32,721
Where's Chiara now?

250
00:24:36,224 --> 00:24:38,059
Viktor, during your brief conversation
with Chiara,

251
00:24:38,143 --> 00:24:39,477
did she mention anything?

252
00:24:41,229 --> 00:24:42,063
Did she mention anyone?

253
00:24:42,147 --> 00:24:43,148
Anything at all.

254
00:24:43,231 --> 00:24:45,025
A person, someone she knew, or an event.

255
00:24:45,609 --> 00:24:47,402
Nothing, Agent Alex.

256
00:25:30,528 --> 00:25:31,738
Chiara is missing.

257
00:25:31,821 --> 00:25:33,073
I don’t know where to start.

258
00:25:33,156 --> 00:25:35,617
But maybe you have to rest first.

259
00:25:35,700 --> 00:25:37,118
But we’re wasting so much time!

260
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:39,037
I think Tess is right.

261
00:25:39,120 --> 00:25:40,330
You better rest first.

262
00:25:40,413 --> 00:25:44,459
Mom. Chiara might be in more danger
if we stop searching.

263
00:25:48,213 --> 00:25:50,215
<i>I have so many secrets to hide</i>

264
00:25:50,298 --> 00:25:54,052
<i>just to give our family</i>
<i>a simple life, Mikoy.</i>

265
00:25:54,135 --> 00:25:57,514
<i>Because of that, I feel like</i>
<i>fate is making me pay.</i>

266
00:25:58,098 --> 00:26:01,476
<i>Only if you knew, it’s so hard</i>
<i>for me to see you suffer.</i>

267
00:26:01,559 --> 00:26:03,228
<i>You’re a good person, my son.</i>

268
00:26:03,311 --> 00:26:05,438
<i>And I will do everything just to help you.</i>

269
00:26:06,898 --> 00:26:08,400
<i>Sean is talking to someone suspicious.</i>

270
00:26:08,483 --> 00:26:11,111
<i>There’s a new character</i>
<i>in Chiara and Mikoy’s life.</i>

271
00:26:11,194 --> 00:26:13,363
And now she’s a running away bride?

272
00:26:16,616 --> 00:26:19,286
This Vicky should be investigated.

273
00:26:20,578 --> 00:26:22,747
Is there’s still no news
about my daughter?

274
00:26:22,831 --> 00:26:24,082
For now, none.

275
00:26:24,165 --> 00:26:27,002
Chiara is not someone
who will just disappear.

276
00:26:27,085 --> 00:26:28,628
I think there’s something that happened.
